mpd-discplayer (0.9.0) trixie; urgency=low

  * Add --eject CLI action: stop disc playback, remove the CD tracks from
    the queue and eject the disc
  * Mount USB devices already plugged in at startup, without autoplay
  * Keep MPD mounts of devices still plugged in at startup and only clear
    stale udisks mounts, other storages (nfs, smb) are left untouched
  * Skip MPD mount when the label is already mounted
  * Reuse a valid symlink kept from a previous run
  * Document CLI options
  * Bump golang.org/x/sys to 0.49.0, oto to 3.5.1 and pulse to 0.1.3
  * CI: build with Go 1.25, lint with Go 1.26, actions/setup-go 7

 -- Mathieu Réquillart <mathieu.requillart@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200


mpd-discplayer (0.8.0) trixie; urgency=low

  * Update go-disc-cuer to v0.4.0 (refactored Generator API):
    - GNUDB: rejoin track titles split over several TTITLE lines
    - MusicBrainz: guard against empty release data
    - Redact the GNUDB hello= email from logged URLs
  * Add a golangci-lint and gofmt CI workflow and fix its findings
  * Bump golang.org/x/sys to 0.47.0 and pulse to 0.1.2

 -- Mathieu Réquillart <mathieu.requillart@gmail.com>  Wed, 08 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0200


mpd-discplayer (0.7.3) trixie; urgency=low

  * Fall back to the UUID when a USB device has no filesystem label
  * Retry MPD mount to handle udisks neighbor registration delay
  * Find MPD neighbor by UUID or serial instead of UUID only
  * Split mount/unmount into MPD and OS-specific methods
  * Check the filesystem type when the partition entry type is unavailable
  * Document the polkit rule for headless systems
  * Bump golang.org/x/sys to 0.42.0

 -- Mathieu Réquillart <mathieu.requillart@gmail.com>  Wed, 01 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0200


